# The short proof on Windows (Maat 1.5.1): the quick suites in Git Bash, about 50 minutes in all, instead of the whole
# Windows part of the full run (about 10 hours). `bash tools/giro-completo.sh --windows-breve …` runs these lines in this
# order; each entry must be in tools/suite.list. A line: [VAR=value …] <entry>. The real Windows proof moves to the
# multi-platform CI (1.5.3). Seconds measured in Git Bash in the 1.5.0 full run (machine shared with other sessions).
tools/suite.test.sh
stop-hook
blocks-independent
phase-usage
session-start
harness-merge
phase-events
maat-config
context-pack
genericita
senza-wsl
maat-paths
messages
cycle-report
guard
bash-node
test-review-surface
gates
# total ≈ 2900 s (≈ 48 min): 35 10 16 19 33 47 57 70 94 125 136 200 213 232 247 248 270 826.
# Left out: ROLLBACK_TEST_RAPIDO=1 rollback (≈ 3100 s, 52 min, measured for 1.5.1): with it the proof would take
# about 1 h 40 min. Run it by hand when a release touches the wrappers (docs/TESTING-harness.md, «The short proof on
# Windows»); to add it here, the line is: ROLLBACK_TEST_RAPIDO=1 rollback
